    "reviewed_content": [
      "Reviewed all seven formal entry pages plus the blessing map, ranged weapon reverse index, catalog indexes, and translation glossary in the fixed 29-file scope; every file hash matches the frozen scope.",
      "Confirmed the actual single trait and two bindings (plasmagun_p1_m1 / M35 Magnacore Mk II and plasmagun_p1_m2 / M35 Magnacore Mk III), ranged classification, shared tier behavior, weapon-page backlinks, and icon attachment/path identity.",
      "Confirmed I–IV factors 0.96/0.94/0.92/0.90 replace the same-key 0.9 wrapper fallback, with effective count clamped to five and multiplicative p^n aggregation; five-step reductions and tier table values are arithmetically correct.",
      "Confirmed actual action-chain scope: linked shoot_hit_scan actions increment; linked direct/brace charge holds the current count; the accepted 15-range follow-up correctly qualifies fresh manual starts because ActionHandler early-resets before hold/increase when no running action and keep_combo_on_start is absent. The .5-second idle reset, reload/vent/unwield clearing and first updated-cache effect are described without promising retroactive heat changes.",
      "Confirmed selected shot and charge heat producers use overheat_amount with their stage multipliers; natural dissipation, vent speed, and charge duration are separate consumers and are not claimed to improve.",
      "Confirmed all four exact EN/ZH tier reconstructions and formatter order. English “reduces ... by -X%” is identified as a signed-direction contradiction; the Chinese fragment is described as missing an explicit verb without inferring the opposite effect.",
      "Confirmed examples distinguish normalized H=0.20 from 20 heat-meter percentage points, show IV one/five-step outputs, and correctly compute q=0.80 compound output 0.0944784 from baseline 0.16 with a 40.951% relative reduction under stated no-lockout/no-cap assumptions.",
      "Root focused source, link and GFM receipts pass with no new errors; no FASTER support is claimed."
    ],
